{"name":"Indian Mesa","hex":"#d5a193","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"indian","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Indian (“indigene”)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Indian (“indigenous”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indian"},{"term":"mesa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat area of land higher than other land, with one or more clifflike edges.","a structure with components rising above the insulating substrate that surrounds it"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mesa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Indian Mesa","blocks":[{"text":"Indian Mesa is a flat top hill whose sides are steep cliffs. Indian Mesa is located within the Lake Pleasant Regional Park grounds by the shores of Lake Pleasant and Agua Fria River in the Bradshaw Mountain Range. Lake Pleasant Regional Park is within the municipal boundaries of Peoria, Arizona. On top of the mesa there are ruins of a prehistoric Hohokam village which is monitored by the Arizona Site Stewards and considered an important archaeological site by the U.S. Bureau of Land Management. There is a small, steep and narrow path which begins at the skirt of the hill and leads to the top of the mesa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Indian_Mesa.JPG/330px-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Indian_Mesa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Mesa","wikidata":"Q16242347"},{"title":"Mesa","blocks":[{"text":"A mesa is an isolated, flat-topped elevation, ridge, or hill, bounded from all sides by steep escarpments and standing distinctly above a surrounding plain. Mesas consist of flat-lying soft sedimentary rocks, such as shales, capped by a resistant layer of harder rock, like sandstone or limestone, forming a caprock that protects the flat summit. The caprock may also include dissected lava flows or eroded duricrust."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Over_Monument_Valley%2C_Navajo_Nation.jpg/330px-Over_Monument_Valley%2C_Navajo_Nation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesa","wikidata":"Q623319"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Indian_Mesa_Ruins_Marker.jpg/250px-Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Indian_Mesa_Ruins_Marker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Indian_Mesa_Ruins_Marker.jpg/500px-Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Indian_Mesa_Ruins_Marker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Indian_Mesa_Ruins_Marker.jpg/250px-Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Indian_Mesa_Ruins_Marker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APeoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Indian_Mesa_Ruins_Marker.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Hiking_trail.jpg/250px-Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Hiking_trail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Hiking_trail.jpg/500px-Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Hiking_trail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Hiking_trail.jpg/250px-Peoria-Lake_Pleasant_Regional_Park-Hiking_trail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam